c-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8804em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>It’s quick, but all the noise of just two readings goes straight into <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"least-squares-over-many-points\">Least squares over many points</h2>\n<p>With <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span></span> references, stack the model as <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">r</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.0319em;\">θ</span></span></span></span></span></span> with rows <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mclose\">]</span></span></span></span> and solve the normal equations from Phase 01:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord boldsymbol\" style=\"margin-right:0.0319em;\">θ</span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1491em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">⊤</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8641em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">⊤</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">r</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>The noise averages out, and you get <strong>residuals</strong> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8444em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.1944em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0278em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> to inspect:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Residuals that look random, with an rms near the sensor noise, mean the model fits.</li>\n<li>A curved pattern (a bow) means non-linearity. Add a quadratic column <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0728em;vertical-align:-0.2587em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4413em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2587em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, or calibrate piecewise.</li>\n<li>One large residual is an outlier: a bad reference or a misread.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Spread the reference points across the whole range, and include the ends. Extrapolating outside the calibrated range is a guess.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"lsq\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>The same least-squares fit applied to a motor’s torque constant. Add noise or reduce the samples and watch the fitted slope’s error grow.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A load cell reads 1012 counts empty and 53 412 counts with a 5.000 kg reference.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Two-point: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.625em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">53</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">412</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1012</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">480</span></span></span></span> counts/kg and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">o</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1012</span></span></span></span> counts.</li>\n<li>A reading of 22 000 counts gives <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord katex-accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"accent-body\" style=\"left:-0.25em;\"><span class=\"mord\">^</span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">22</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">000</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1012</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">/10</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">480</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">2.0027</span></span></span></span> kg.</li>\n<li>If each reading has 20 counts rms noise, the two-point slope has an uncertainty of about <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.04em;vertical-align:-0.1328em;\"></span><span class=\"mord sqrt\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.9072em;\"><span class=\"svg-align\" style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\" style=\"padding-left:0.833em;\">2</span></span><span style=\"top:-2.8672em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"hide-tail\" style=\"min-width:0.853em;height:1.08em;\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"400em\" height=\"1.08em\" viewBox=\"0 0 400000 1080\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMinYMin slice\"><path d=\"M95,702\nc-2.7,0,-7.17,-2.7,-13.5,-8c-5.8,-5.3,-9.5,-10,-9.5,-14\nc0,-2,0.3,-3.3,1,-4c1.3,-2.7,23.83,-20.7,67.5,-54\nc44.2,-33.3,65.8,-50.3,66.5,-51c1.3,-1.3,3,-2,5,-2c4.7,0,8.7,3.3,12,10\ns173,378,173,378c0.7,0,35.3,-71,104,-213c68.7,-142,137.5,-285,206.5,-429\nc69,-144,104.5,-217.7,106.5,-221\nl0 -0\nc5.3,-9.3,12,-14,20,-14\nH400000v40H845.2724\ns-225.272,467,-225.272,467s-235,486,-235,486c-2.7,4.7,-9,7,-19,7\nc-6,0,-10,-1,-12,-3s-194,-422,-194,-422s-65,47,-65,47z\nM834 80h400000v40h-400000z\"/></svg></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1328em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20/5</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5.7</span></span></span></span> counts/kg, or 0.054 % of the slope.</li>\n<li>Each single reading also carries the noise: 20 counts is 1.9 g. Averaging 16 samples per reading brings it to 0.5 g.</li>\n<li>A least-squares fit over 11 points (0 to 5 kg in 0.5 kg steps) cuts that by about 2.5× and shows any bow in the residuals.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">calibrate.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>)\nG_TRUE, O_TRUE, BOW, NOISE = <span class=\"hljs-number\">10_480.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1012.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">30.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># counts/kg, counts, counts at mid-scale, counts rms</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">load_cell</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">m</span>):\n    x = np.asarray(m) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> G_TRUE * np.asarray(m) + O_TRUE + BOW * <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span> * x * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> - x) + NOISE * rng.standard_normal(np.shape(m))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">fit</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">m, r, quadratic=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span></span>):\n    cols = [m, np.ones_like(m)] + ([m**<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>] <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> quadratic <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span> [])\n    A = np.column_stack(cols)\n    theta = np.linalg.solve(A.T @ A, A.T @ r)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> theta, r - A @ theta\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">invert</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">theta, r</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(theta) == <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>:\n        g, o = theta\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (r - o) / g\n    g, o, q = theta                                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># q m^2 + g m + o = r</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> (-g + np.sqrt(g * g - <span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span> * q * (o - r))) / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> * q)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    refs = np.linspace(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">11</span>)\n    r = load_cell(refs)\n    two = np.array([(r[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] - r[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]) / <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, r[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]])\n    lin, res_lin = fit(refs, r)\n    quad, res_q = fit(refs, r, quadratic=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">True</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;two-point g, o:&quot;</span>, two.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot; least squares:&quot;</span>, lin.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot; residual rms:&quot;</span>, res_lin.std().<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>), <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;-&gt;&quot;</span>, res_q.std().<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># the linear fit leaves a bow: residuals at the ends and middle have opposite signs</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> res_lin[<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>] &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> res_lin[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> res_lin[-<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>] &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> res_q.std() &lt; res_lin.std()\n    <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># check against the spec on fresh readings, each the mean of 16 samples: |error| &lt; 0.1 % of full scale (5 g)</span>\n    test_m = rng.uniform(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">500</span>)\n    test_r = np.mean([load_cell(test_m) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">16</span>)], axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>)\n    err = invert(quad, test_r) - test_m\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;after quadratic calibration: max error <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span>*np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>():<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> g&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(err).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.005</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(invert(np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">10_480.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1012.0</span>]), <span class=\"hljs-number\">22_000</span>) - <span class=\"hljs-number\">2.0027</span>) &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">1e-4</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Your residuals after a linear fit are about +3, −1, −4, −1, +3 counts at 0, 25, 50, 75 and 100 % of the range. What does that tell you?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>A symmetric bow: the sensor is non-linear (curved), not just noisy. Fit a quadratic term, or calibrate with a lookup table.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why should calibration references span the whole working range?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>The fit is only trustworthy where it has data. Outside it, slope errors grow with the distance, and any non-linearity goes unseen.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p07-l02\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"two-points-define-a-line","title":"Two points define a line"},{"id":"least-squares-over-many-points","title":"Least squares over many points"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p07-l02-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Gain in counts/kg from 1012 counts at 0 kg and 53 412 counts at 5 kg?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Rise over run.</p>\n","answer":10480,"tol":0.001,"unit":"counts/kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Mass in kg for a reading of 22 000 counts?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Subtract the offset, divide by the gain.</p>\n","answer":2.00267,"tol":0.001,"unit":"kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Residuals that form a smooth bow indicate…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Noise doesn’t have a shape.</p>\n","options":["random noise","non-linearity the model doesn’t capture","a perfect fit","an offset error"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l02-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Least squares improves on a two-point calibration because…</p>\n","explain":"<p>More data and a diagnostic.</p>\n","options":["it needs no references","noise averages over many points, and residuals can be inspected","it is always exact","it removes hysteresis"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l02-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Uncertainty in counts/kg of a two-point slope over 5 kg with 20 counts rms noise per reading?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Two independent readings.</p>\n","answer":5.657,"tol":0.002,"unit":"counts/kg"},{"id":"p07-l02-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>0.1 % of a 5 kg full scale in grams?</p>\n","explain":"<p>The spec used in the code.</p>\n","answer":5,"tol":0.001,"unit":"g"}],"code":[{"file":"calibrate.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(4)\nG_TRUE, O_TRUE, BOW, NOISE = 10_480.0, 1012.0, 30.0, 20.0     # counts/kg, counts, counts at mid-scale, counts rms\n\ndef load_cell(m):\n    x = np.asarray(m) / 5.0\n    return G_TRUE * np.asarray(m) + O_TRUE + BOW * 4 * x * (1 - x) + NOISE * rng.standard_normal(np.shape(m))\n\ndef fit(m, r, quadratic=False):\n    cols = [m, np.ones_like(m)] + ([m**2] if quadratic else [])\n    A = np.column_stack(cols)\n    theta = np.linalg.solve(A.T @ A, A.T @ r)\n    return theta, r - A @ theta\n\ndef invert(theta, r):\n    if len(theta) == 2:\n        g, o = theta\n        return (r - o) / g\n    g, o, q = theta                                            # q m^2 + g m + o = r\n    return (-g + np.sqrt(g * g - 4 * q * (o - r))) / (2 * q)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    refs = np.linspace(0, 5, 11)\n    r = load_cell(refs)\n    two = np.array([(r[-1] - r[0]) / 5, r[0]])\n    lin, res_lin = fit(refs, r)\n    quad, res_q = fit(refs, r, quadratic=True)\n    print(\"two-point g, o:\", two.round(1), \" least squares:\", lin.round(1), \" residual rms:\", res_lin.std().round(1), \"->\", res_q.std().round(1))\n    # the linear fit leaves a bow: residuals at the ends and middle have opposite signs\n    assert res_lin[5] > 0 and res_lin[0] < 0 and res_lin[-1] < 0\n    assert res_q.std() < res_lin.std()\n    # check against the spec on fresh readings, each the mean of 16 samples: |error| < 0.1 % of full scale (5 g)\n    test_m = rng.uniform(0, 5, 500)\n    test_r = np.mean([load_cell(test_m) for _ in range(16)], axis=0)\n    err = invert(quad, test_r) - test_m\n    print(f\"after quadratic calibration: max error {1000*np.abs(err).max():.2f} g\")\n    assert np.abs(err).max() < 0.005\n    assert np.abs(invert(np.array([10_480.0, 1012.0]), 22_000) - 2.0027) < 1e-4"}]}